Workaround that I verified: before retrying, replace the model object so that the form value changes, for example `model.update((m) => ({...m}))`. That clears the submission error, and the next Send runs the action. Another option is to catch network errors inside the action and show them with your own signal instead of returning them, but then they are not form errors.

Not tested: other browsers, zone.js apps.

### Which @angular/* package(s) are the source of the bug?

zone.js

### Is this a regression?

No

### Description


zone.js forwards an unhandled ZoneAwarePromise rejection to `unhandledrejection` listeners registered on `window` through `findPromiseRejectionHandler` in `packages/zone.js/lib/browser/browser.ts` (zone.js 0.16.3, as in the Angular v22.2.6 tree):

```ts
// lib/browser/browser.ts, findPromiseRejectionHandler (line 313)
const evt = new PromiseRejectionEvent(evtName, {
  promise: e.promise,
  reason: e.rejection,
});
eventTask.invoke(evt);
```

A listener added to `window` with the patched `addEventListener` is an event task created with `useG: true` (`OPTIMIZED_ZONE_EVENT_TASK_DATA`, `lib/common/events.ts` line 84), and for such a task the `ZoneTask` constructor does not make a closure:

```ts
// lib/zone-impl.ts, ZoneTask constructor (lines 1417-1418)
if (type === eventTask && options && (options as any).useG) {
  this.invoke = ZoneTask.invokeTask;
}
```

`ZoneTask.invokeTask` is the static `invokeTask(task, target, args)` (line 1426), so `eventTask.invoke(evt)` passes the event as the task: `task.zone.runTask(...)` throws a TypeError because `evt.zone` is undefined. `handleUnhandledRejection` (`lib/common/promise.ts` line 82) swallows the error with `catch (err) {}`, so the listener is never called and nothing is reported.

zone.js's own global event callback calls the same function with the task first: `task.invoke(task, target, [event])` (`lib/common/events.ts` line 239). Calling it that way in `findPromiseRejectionHandler`, `eventTask.invoke(eventTask, global, [evt])`, looks like the fix for `useG` tasks. That is a suggestion only; we have not tested it against the suite.

#### Why the zone.js test still passes in Chrome and Safari

`packages/zone.js/test/common/zone.spec.ts`, "should surface unhandled promise rejections via unhandledrejection event (if the flag is enabled)", passes in Chrome and Safari for a different reason. In those two browsers `PromiseRejectionEventInit.promise` is still typed `Promise<any>` (Blink `third_party/blink/renderer/core/events/promise_rejection_event_init.idl`; WebKit `Source/WebCore/dom/PromiseRejectionEvent.idl`). So `new PromiseRejectionEvent(..., {promise: zoneAwarePromise})` resolves the ZoneAwarePromise thenable into a new native promise, which rejects with the same reason, and nothing handles it. The browser itself then fires a native `unhandledrejection` with that native promise, and the listener receives that event. The `An error was thrown in a Promise outside a test` line in Chrome's test log is jasmine's handler seeing the same native rejection.

The HTML Standard changed the member to `required object promise` in whatwg/html#9897 (merged 2023-12-12). Firefox ships that (`dom/webidl/PromiseRejectionEvent.webidl`), so no native promise is made and the listener is never called. whatwg/html#11547 records that Chrome and Safari still differ from the spec here. As soon as a browser follows the current spec, the test fails there, and zone.js applications never receive `unhandledrejection` for ZoneAwarePromise rejections. That happens in Firefox today, and in any browser engine that follows the current spec, as Firefox does.


### Related issues

#51357 and #55590 report that `new PromiseRejectionEvent(...)` in the same function throws when `e.promise` is undefined, which happens when `DISABLE_WRAPPING_UNCAUGHT_PROMISE_REJECTION` is `true` (the default since #52492). This report is the failure behind that one: with the flag `false`, as zone.js's own browser tests set it, the event constructs, and dispatch then fails at `eventTask.invoke(evt)`. Fixing the constructor's input alone will not make listeners fire.

**Expected:** zone.js calls the listener with the event it built (its `promise` is the ZoneAwarePromise, `reason` is `'Error happened :('`) in every browser, whatever the browser's `PromiseRejectionEventInit` type.

### Please provide a link to a minimal reproduction of the bug

Self-contained page below (no link needed).


Serve this page next to `zone.umd.js` (zone.js 0.16.3, `bundles/zone.umd.js`) from any static HTTP server and open it. The first script sets the same flag the zone.js browser tests set (`test/browser-zone-setup.ts`).

```html
<!doctype html><body>
<script>window.__zone_symbol__DISABLE_WRAPPING_UNCAUGHT_PROMISE_REJECTION = false;</script>
<script src="zone.umd.js"></script>
<script>
const log = (...a) => console.log(a.map(String).join(' '));
window.onerror = () => {};
const sym = Zone.__symbol__('unhandledPromiseRejectionHandler');
const orig = Zone[sym];
// Only records whether zone.js's own dispatch throws; it constructs no event itself.
Zone[sym] = function (e) {
  try { orig.call(this, e); log('zone dispatch returned'); } catch (err) { log('zone dispatch threw: ' + err); }
};
window[Zone.__symbol__('enable_native_microtask_draining')] = true;
let calls = 0;
Zone.current.fork({name: 'probe'}).run(() => {
  window.addEventListener('unhandledrejection', (e) => {
    calls++;
    log('listener call ' + calls + ': reason=' + e.reason +
        ' native promise=' + (e.promise instanceof window[Zone.__symbol__('Promise')]));
  });
  const s = document.createElement('script');
  s.innerHTML = "Promise.reject('Error happened :(')";
  document.body.append(s);
});
setTimeout(() => log('result: listener calls=' + calls), 100);
</script>
```

The wrapper calls the original handler inside a `try`, so the TypeError that zone.js swallows shows up in the console.

#### Results (2026-11-22)

| Browser | zone.js's dispatch | listener calls |
|---|---|---|
| Chrome for Testing 157 | `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'runTask')` | 1: the event's promise is a native promise, not the ZoneAwarePromise |
| Safari 27.0 | `TypeError: undefined is not an object (evaluating 'task.zone.runTask')` | 1: the event's promise is a native promise |
| Firefox 159.0 | `TypeError: can't access property "runTask", task.zone is undefined` | 0 |

zone.js's own dispatch throws in all three browsers. Chrome and Safari call the listener only through the native rejection that their `Promise<any>` conversion creates.


